{
  "results": [
    {
      "n": "G1",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show the 3D scene rendered cleanly in Chrome with no blank screen or errors.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G2",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 2–5 demonstrate orbiting and zooming, and `OrbitControls` restricts `maxPolarAngle = Math.PI * 0.465` and `maxDistance = 15.5`, keeping the camera above the cloth (`PlaneGeometry(34, 34)`). However, at max distance with shallow polar angles (screenshot 5), the back edge of the cloth is visible against a black void.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "G3",
      "evidence": "Scene geometry is modest (~30k triangles, one `InstancedMesh`, one `Points` cloud), with two shadow maps (2048 and 1024) and `BokehPass` + `UnrealBloomPass` + transmission pass; on a standard laptop with integrated graphics, `BokehPass` + `MeshPhysicalMaterial` transmission at up to 2x DPR can dip near 30 fps, though overall draw call count (~45) is light enough to stay around 30+ fps.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "1",
      "evidence": "All screenshots (1–5) display a bottom UI bar (`#ui`) containing text ('Drag to orbit · Scroll to zoom') and two interactive buttons ('Macro DoF: ON' and 'Hero Angle').",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "2",
      "evidence": "In the `animate()` loop in the HTML source, only `controls.update()`, camera reset lerping, and `bokehPass` focus distance updates occur; there is no environmental motion running on load.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "3",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 shows a close-up, slightly elevated angle with the French toast stack centered on the dark plate, closely matching the framing of the reference photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "4",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–3 show three thick slices of French toast stacked and slightly offset/rotated relative to each other, matching the arrangement in the photo.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "5",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show banana slices placed between the toast layers, on top, and around the base on the plate, though several slices in screenshot 1 clip heavily into the toast and plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "6",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show blueberries clustered on top of the stack, tucked between slices, and scattered at the front base on the plate.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "7",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the stack resting on a dark round plate set upon a grey-beige cloth surface.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "8",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show white sugar particles scattered across the dark plate and lightly dusted on the top toast slice and berries.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "9",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast slices look like corrugated plastic crackers or wavy tart shells with uniform vertical fluting all around the perimeter and smooth, bright yellow flat centers, rather than thick slices of bread with a rounded loaf crust and soft cut faces as in the photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "10",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 4 show round banana discs with a faint dark 3-part seeded pattern in the center, though translucent syrup artifacts overlap parts of them.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "11",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–4 show round blueberries of slightly varying sizes (`r: 0.250` to `0.315` in `berryPlacements`) with sculpted 5-pointed star crowns visible at their tops.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "12",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 2, a blueberry under the middle slice (`[-1.18, 1.44, 0.56]`) and overhanging banana slices visibly float or protrude awkwardly without proper support, and in screenshot 1 syrup drips hang in mid-air.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "13",
      "evidence": "When orbited in screenshots 2, 3, and 4, the toast, plate, and cloth are closed meshes, though in screenshots 1–4 there is a harsh circular rendering artifact ring on the plate and severe transmission sorting holes/cutouts through the bananas and toast.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "14",
      "evidence": "In the reference photo, soft window light comes from behind and to the left (back-left), whereas in the code `keyLight.position.set(-5.2, 8.4, 5.4)` places the main key light in front and to the left (`+z` is toward the camera at `z = 8.15`), lighting the front crust flatly instead of backlighting it.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "15",
      "evidence": "In screenshot 1, despite `BokehPass` being enabled (`maxblur: 0.0065`), the back plate rim and the horizon edge of the cloth against the black background remain quite sharp and clearly defined rather than softly blurred as in the reference photo.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "16",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1–5 show very little soft contact shadowing grounding the blueberries, bananas, and toast layers against each other or the dark plate, leaving items looking pasted on.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "17",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1, 2, 3, and 5, the entire upper background strip above the tablecloth (`scene.background = new THREE.Color(0x161412)` / black void) renders as a solid near-black band across the top of the frame.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "18",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–3, the syrup rivulets on the crust look like dark brown opaque/plastic worms with dull highlights, and the syrup puddles on the plate look like flat reddish-brown shapes or cause weird grey circular refraction glitches on the bananas.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "19",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the toast has uniform, smooth, cartoon-like yellow centers and repetitive striped brown edges with no visible porous bread crumb texture.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "20",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the blueberries have harsh, high-contrast blotchy white-grey and black marbling that looks like polished granite or camouflage rather than a soft, dusty matte wax bloom.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "21",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, the banana slices look flat, chalky grey-white, and suffer from sharp dark/grey circular clipping or transmission artifacts rather than looking moist and slightly translucent.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "22",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the plate has a distracting bright thin circular ring artifact on its floor, and the cloth reads as a blurry grey-beige ground plane rather than clearly woven linen fabric.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "23",
      "evidence": "Screenshots 1 and 5 show the plate and tablecloth sitting level and horizontal with no unintended tilt.",
      "pass": true
    },
    {
      "n": "24",
      "evidence": "Checking `addCrustSyrupRivulets` and `animate()` in the code confirms the syrup rivulets are static `TubeGeometry` meshes with no dripping or running animation.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "25",
      "evidence": "There is no steam or warm haze particle system or shader anywhere in the HTML source or visible in screenshots 1–5.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "26",
      "evidence": "There is no continuous environmental motion in `animate()` at all.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "27",
      "evidence": "Although vertex seeds vary slightly, `berryMat` shares a single `berryTex` UV texture across all berries, making identical blotchy texture patterns appear on adjacent berries in screenshots 1 and 4.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "28",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–4, multiple banana slices and blueberries visibly clip/intersect straight into the toast crusts and into the plate floor (e.g., the upright front bananas and top bananas).",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "29",
      "evidence": "In screenshots 1–5, the sugar on the plate appears as large, coarse, isolated bright white dots/pellets rather than fine, soft powdered sugar.",
      "pass": false
    },
    {
      "n": "30",
      "evidence": "Screenshot 1 looks distinctly stylized and synthetic—with corrugated plastic-looking toast, blotchy granite-like berries, coarse white dots, clipping artifacts, a black sky bar, and an on-screen UI bar—and could not pass for the reference photo at first glance.",
      "pass": false
    }
  ]
}
